# Line endings, so Godot's own files stop showing as modified on Windows.
#
# Godot writes .import, .tres, .tscn and project.godot with LF. A Windows
# checkout without this rewrites them to CRLF the first time the editor touches
# them, and fifty audio .import files sit in `git status` forever with ZERO
# content changes — measured: `git diff --numstat` reports no changed lines on
# any of them. That noise is not harmless. It buries the files somebody
# actually edited, which is exactly how a real change gets committed by
# accident or missed entirely.
#
# eol=lf rather than text=auto: half these files are written by the engine and
# half by hand, and `auto` decides per file from its current contents, which is
# how a repository ends up with both conventions and no way to tell which was
# intended.
*.import    text eol=lf
*.gd        text eol=lf
*.gdshader  text eol=lf
*.tres      text eol=lf
*.tscn      text eol=lf
*.cfg       text eol=lf
*.godot     text eol=lf
*.uid       text eol=lf

*.md        text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.js        text eol=lf
*.mjs       text eol=lf

# Marked so a checkout never tries to translate them. A single byte changed in
# a PNG is a corrupt sprite, not a whitespace nit.
*.png       binary
*.ogg       binary
*.wav       binary
*.ttf       binary
*.otf       binary
